{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>הנחמים [those who are inflamed].</b> The best of the interpretations is that it speaks of idolatry, and הנחמים is on the pattern of הנצבים (Genesis 45:1), from the nif'al binyan, from the root of בכל יחם הצאן (Genesis 30:41), and behold it is joined with ילדי פשע, and behold it is written, ובחטא יחמתני אמי (Psalms 51:7)." "<b>שוחטי [those who slaughter].</b> For idolatry, like ואשחט אותם (Genesis 40:11), like the deed of the prostitute who kills her children." "<b>בחלקי.</b> From the root of חלוקי אבנים (1 Samuel 17:40), and the meaning is that they seek smooth stones to engrave them to be carved images."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 57, :notes {2 "MS note צ״ל חלקות indicates the scribe corrects חלקים to חלקות; I translate the corrected reading."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:59.694661760Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}